messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/libtests/readpng.c
Line: 95
Function: read_png
Bug type: out-of-bounds-write
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: display is mistakenly declared as a png_byte (byte) at line 37 instead of a png_bytep (pointer). It is then assigned malloc(rowbytes) at line 65, which truncates the pointer to a byte, and passed to png_read_row as the third argument at line 95, where a pointer is expected. This results in writes through an invalid pointer, causing memory corruption or a crash. The same mistake also leads to calling free(display) on an invalid pointer in the cleanup paths.

Source context:
```c
